Z||000006||kidzwheelz||02-09-2000||11:55 AM||||   SCCA, I have only driven my Fiero one time, it was a very short trip up the street and back in which a lot of swearing was heard. (probably a premature trip) You see, I bought a basket case '84 for $220. Some minor repairs were required. After a complete engine rebuild, new clutch, new brakes, and a thorough investigation of what the previous owner was smoking, I was able to make a maiden voyage on two gears, questionable clutch, and brakes. But hey, autocross you say? What the hell, I'll try anything once! ||||reg||3
Z||000007||SCCA FIERO||02-09-2000||08:39 PM||||I kinda suspected that was you, but wasn't sure. I remember you from the autocross (member I got stung by that damn bee?). How do you like those window scoops? I got a fastback clip for my Fiero and it needs 1/4 windows. Can you see through them? I think I am gonna get clear factory type but not sure... I don't want "GT" on them cuz, well, I don't have a GT. I am gonna have an 88 Coupe, fastback, V6 with GT wheels  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">. <P>I talk to Karl all the time... he sold his GT (did I tell ya that already?) He has no Fiero right now, but His girlfriend has a purple 86GT that he might autocross this year.<P>As far as my Fiero goes... I haven't driven it for a few months. I got a set of Centerlines for it and I think I found a 1 inch rear swaybar. I also got poly for the front suspension, but haven't got off my lazy butt and installed them and also got poly dogbone bushings. It has an oil leak that I tried to fix, but failed  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">. It should be ready by the first autocross.<BR>||||reg||6
Z||000008||FIEROCIOUS||02-10-2000||12:36 AM||||The side window vents are fiberglass. You can't see out of them. BIG blind spot! But I like them I'm glad I didn't just replace my broken glass with the stock window. They were a pain in the tush to install, The Fiero store gave me double sticky tape to install them (doesn't work) so I fiberglassed them in. For the first few months I was paranoid they would fall out, but they're still in no signs of them coming out now I'm more worried about ever getting them off if I ever wanted to! You can't fiberglass the lexan plastic ones! You saw Karls windows (falling off!) Hey how did Karl do his hood? Did he cut the cross member?<BR>Kidzwheelz I dare you to come out and play!<BR>One more person to kick around on the track!<BR>I'll run circles around ya!LOL! ||||reg||1
Z||000009||SCCA FIERO||02-10-2000||11:31 PM||||Karl bought that green and white GT like it was... hoodscoop was already in it. The thicker part of the hood was not cut, but the hood did twist if you didn't lift it in the middle and the scoop was breaking apart. It was very nice though. Karl and I tried to make one out of the 6 extra hoods we had but couldn't make it work.<P>Kidzwheelz, I think I know where you could pick up 2 or 3 84's very cheap if you need parts. There is a place on Washington around 32nd that has a few. They sell crappy cars and have 3(I think 3) 84s in the back and an 85SE V6 on the lot. The 85 runs but needs a clutch... don't know about the 84s. ||||reg||1
